Refining the influence map...
Influence_map: The notation [i -> j] means an agent at position [i] of the first rule/var has an influence to an agent at position [j] of the second rule/var.
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(0):'' A(a[.]),B(x[.])->A(a[1]),B(x[1]) -> rule(1):'' A(a[1],b{u}),B(x[1],y{u})->A(a[1],b{p}),B(x[1],y{p})[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(0):'' A(a[.]),B(x[.])->A(a[1]),B(x[1]) -> rule(2):'' A(a[1],b{p}),B(x[1],y{p})->A(a[1],b{u}),B(x[1],y{u})[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(0):'' A(a[.]),B(x[.])->A(a[1]),B(x[1]) -> rule(8):'not_sym1' A(a[1],b{p}),B(x[1],y{u})->.,.[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(0):'' A(a[.]),B(x[.])->A(a[1]),B(x[1]) -> rule(9):'not_sym2' A(a[1],b{u}),B(x[1],y{p})->.,.[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(1):'' A(a[1],b{u}),B(x[1],y{u})->A(a[1],b{p}),B(x[1],y{p}) -> rule(2):'' A(a[1],b{p}),B(x[1],y{p})->A(a[1],b{u}),B(x[1],y{u})[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(2):'' A(a[1],b{p}),B(x[1],y{p})->A(a[1],b{u}),B(x[1],y{u}) -> rule(1):'' A(a[1],b{u}),B(x[1],y{u})->A(a[1],b{p}),B(x[1],y{p})[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(3):'' A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{u})->A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{u}) -> rule(4):'' A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{u})->A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{p})[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(3):'' A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{u})->A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{u}) -> rule(7):'' A(a[1]),C(z[1]),B(x[.])->A(a[1]),C(z[.]),B(x[1])[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(4):'' A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{u})->A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{p}) -> rule(0):'' A(a[.]),B(x[.])->A(a[1]),B(x[1])[0->0]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(4):'' A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{u})->A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{p}) -> rule(3):'' A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{u})->A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{u})[0->0]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(4):'' A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{u})->A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{p}) -> rule(5):'' A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{p})->A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{p})[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(5):'' A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{p})->A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{p}) -> rule(6):'' A(a[1],b{u}),C(z[1],k{p})->A(a[1],b{p}),C(z[1],k{p})[0->0];[1->1]
Influence_map:Wake_up_map:rule(5):'' A(a[.]),C(z[.],k{p})->A(a[1]),C(z[1],k{p}) -> rule(7):'' A(a[1]),C(z[1]),B(x[.])->A(a[1]),C(z[.]),B(x[1])[0->0];[1->1]
